id=a52sxq_adreno_driver
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Adreno V@0849 GPU driver (V@0863 selectable)
author=kusti420
description=The A14 vendor ships the Adreno 642L userspace driver V@0530 (Nov 2021). Replace the 64-bit GL/Vulkan/OpenCL stack with a current build of Qualcomm's LA.VENDOR.14.3.4.11 branch plus its a660 SQE microcode: V@0849.0 (09/19/25, from the community module by @sudami) in v849/ is installed; the newer V@0863.1 (12/24/25, "Adreno GPU Driver 863.1" module by @Joshaby) is kept in v863/ but was taken back out of the default after tester feedback - ADRENO_DRIVER at the top of customize.sh selects the set. Both sets have the same 23 files, the same dependencies and the same a660_sqe.fw; the module's extra files (libOpenCL_adreno.so, which nothing on this vendor loads, firmware for other GPUs, its feature xmls and its ro.zygote.disable_gl_preload prop) are not used. The system is 64-bit only and no 32-bit process uses the GPU, so the 32-bit V@0530 libs stay. android.hardware.vulkan.version is raised from the vendor's 1.1 to 1.3, the version the driver reports on the 642L.
